13
00:48:08,888 --> 00:48:14,888
The Descent is a 2005 British horror film written and directed by Neil Marshall.

14
00:51:51,111 --> 00:51:57,111
The film stars actresses Shauna Macdonald, Natalie Mendoza, Alex
Reid, Saskia Mulder, Nora-Jane Noone and MyAnna Buring.

15
00:55:33,333 --> 00:55:39,333
The plot follows six women who enter an uncharted cave system and
struggle to survive against the monstrous creatures inside.

16
00:59:15,555 --> 00:59:21,555
Filming took place in the United Kingdom.

17
01:02:57,777 --> 01:03:03,777
Exterior scenes were filmed at Ashridge Park, Hertfordshire, and in Scotland.

18
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
Because the filmmakers considered it too dangerous and time-consuming to shoot in an actual cave, interior
scenes were filmed on sets built at Pinewood Studios near London designed by Simon Bowles.

19
01:10:22,222 --> 01:10:28,222
The Descent opened in cinemas in the United Kingdom on 8 July 2005.

20
01:14:04,444 --> 01:14:10,444
It premiered in the 2006 Sundance Film Festival and
released on 4 August 2006 in the United States.

21
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
The film received positive reviews with praise for the
performances, cinematography and Marshall's direction.

22
01:21:28,888 --> 01:21:34,888
It was also a box-office success, grossing $57.1 million
worldwide against a £3.5 million budget.

23
01:25:11,111 --> 01:25:17,111
Since its release, it has been regarded as one of
the best horror films of the 2000s.

24
01:28:53,333 --> 01:28:59,333
A sequel, titled The Descent Part 2, was released in 2009.

25
01:32:35,555 --> 01:32:41,555
The film explores themes of panic, darkness, mutant, expedition, cave.

26
01:36:17,777 --> 01:36:23,777
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
